I was accountable for the daily execution of CubIQ MRV reconciliation, a key control for assessing whether the model was ready for production. I used the reconciliation framework to compare approximately 2,500 MRV calculations against the on-premises system and identify discrepancies early in development. The framework surfaced data modeling issues and upstream data defects, including missing columns and incorrect values in ARC. It also exposed performance issues in Power BI and Databricks pipelines that could affect timely processing.

I reported findings to the relevant stakeholders and followed up on remediation. When a discrepancy required a change to calculation logic, I implemented the correction directly in MRV Builder. I ensured that fixes were verified through reconciliation against the agreed acceptance criteria and that the results were supported by evidence.

Running this control daily made it possible to identify issues and act on them throughout development. The reconciliation dashboard gave stakeholders a consolidated view of discrepancies, and the verification evidence helped the team assess whether the model met the criteria for production readiness.
